-- title:
--   Unique prime above a generic supersingular node over a number field
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime, $A$ a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, $k$ a field of characteristic $q$ with decidable equality, and $\mathrm{red}\colon A \to k$ a ring homomorphism. Let $a \in k$ belong to `ssJSet q k`, i.e. every elliptic Weierstrass curve over $k$ with $j$-invariant $a$ has no affine point $P \neq 0$ with $q \cdot P = 0$, and assume $a^{q^2} = a$, $q \ge 5$, $a \neq 0$ and $a \neq 1728$. Let $K \subset \overline{\mathbb Q}$ be a subfield finite over $\mathbb Q$, write $A_0 := A \cap K$ (`coeffSubring A K`) with the induced map $\mathrm{red}_K\colon A_0 \to k$, and assume $a$ lies in the image of $\mathrm{red}_K$. Let $R_0 :=$ `modularLocalizedAtPoint (1 * q) A₀ red_K a (a ^ q)` be the subring of Laurent series over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ consisting of the $f$ for which there are $r, s \in A_0[X_0, X_1]$ with $f \cdot s(j, j_q) = r(j, j_q)$ in Laurent series and $\bar s(a, a^q) \neq 0$, where $r \mapsto r(j,j_q)$ is evaluation at the $q$-expansions `jqModC`, `jqNModC` with $N = 1 \cdot q$ and $\bar r(a,a^q)$ denotes evaluation of $r$ at $(a, a^q)$ after applying $\mathrm{red}_K$ to coefficients. Let $B$ be a subring of the Laurent series with $R_0 \le B$, with $B$ contained in the subfield generated by the constant series from $K$ together with `jqModC` and `jqNModC`, and with every element of $B$ integral over $R_0$. Then any two prime ideals $P_1, P_2$ of $B$ each containing $r(j,j_q)$ for every $r \in A_0[X_0, X_1]$ with $\bar r(a, a^q) = 0$ are equal.
--
--   This is the number-field-coefficient form of the statement that the normalisation of the plane model $\Phi_q(j, j_q) = 0$ over $A \cap K$ has exactly one prime above a generic supersingular node $(a, a^q)$ of its special fibre (Deligne–Rapoport V.1.16 for the normal model of $X_0(q)$, here restricted to $q \ge 5$ and $a \neq 0, 1728$, so that the node has width one). It is used in the construction of the Frobenius node pair attached to such a point, via [`ModularCurve.exists_hasValue_frobNodePair_of_isIntegral_modularLocalizedAtPoint_of_ne_zero_of_ne_1728`](thm.html#ModularCurve.exists_hasValue_frobNodePair_of_isIntegral_modularLocalizedAtPoint_of_ne_zero_of_ne_1728).
